              "size": 0,
              "family": "et-line"
            }
          },
          "title2": "Resume Tip from Ian",
          "subtitle2": "September 29",
          "caption2": "Direct tip for experienced crew: don’t worry about making your CV perfect. You are a professional Captain / Chief Engineer / Chief Stew / Chef, not a professional CV writer. Just communicate what you are bringing to the table.<br>",
          "button2": "<a data-app-btn=\"true\" href=\"https://mobirise.com\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">MORE</a>",
          "media3": {
            "iconFont": {
              "active": true,
              "class": "mbr-iconfont mbr-iconfont-features2",
              "name": "pencil",
              "link": "https://mobirise.com",
              "size": 0,
              "family": "et-line"
            }
          },
          "title3": "Interview Tip from Ian",
          "subtitle3": "September 27",
          "caption3": "Don’t try to figure out your wages on a “per hour” basis. Instead, to get a realistic figure of what you are getting paid, find out what the average person in your age/culture saves as a percentage of their income back home. Look at how much you have in your pocket at the end of the contract. Divide that pocket money by the percentage…you will discover that your average Bosun makes more money than an eye surgeon.",
          "button3": "<a data-app-btn=\"true\" href=\"https://mobirise.com\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">MORE</a>",
          "media4": {
            "iconFont": {
              "active": true,
              "class": "mbr-iconfont mbr-iconfont-features2",
              "name": "global",
              "link": "https://mobirise.com",
              "size": 0,
              "family": "et-line"
            }
          },
          "title4": "Career Tip from Ian",
          "subtitle4": "September 25",
          "caption4": "Never confuse television with reality. Gilligan was not really stuck on the island, Ginger did not have hundreds of dresses, and the Professor never, ever, successfully made a radio out of a coconut in real life.<br>",
          "button4": "<a data-app-btn=\"true\" href=\"https://mobirise.com\" class=\"btn btn-primary\">MORE</a>",
          "media5": {
            "iconFont": {
              "active": true,
              "class": "mbr-iconfont mbr-iconfont-features2",
              "name": "global",
              "link": "https://mobirise.com",
              "size": 0,
              "family": "et-line"
            }
          },
